  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 3. The focal length of a plano-convex lens is equal to its radius
    of curvature. The value of the refractive index of its material is ......
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: "Given focal length, f = R ...... (1)\nWhere, R = Radius of curvature\r\nWe
    know,\r\n1/<i>f</i> = (<i>\u03BC</i> - 1)/R   for a plano-convex lens\r\nPut
    the value of '<i>f</i>' from eq (1):\r\n1/R = (<i>\u03BC</i> - 1)/R\r\n\u21D2
    1 = <i>\u03BC</i> - 1\r\n\r\n\u21D2 <i>\u03BC</i> = <b>2</b>\r\n"
  options:
  - 1
  - 2
  - 1.5
  - 2.5
  correctOptionIndex: 1
